"""Dokku PaaS platform manifest.

Dokku is a Docker-powered, self-hosted mini-Heroku PaaS that runs on a single
Linux server. Developers push code via `git push` over SSH; Dokku auto-detects
the language via Heroku Buildpacks (or a Dockerfile / Nixpacks / Railpack),
builds a container image, and routes HTTP(S) traffic through Nginx.

Architecture reference: https://dokku.com/docs/development/architecture/
Source: https://github.com/dokku/dokku
"""

from scryr import Diagram, Info, Link, Manifest
from scryr.types import (
    Classification,
    DeploymentTarget,
    Markdown,
    MetricTool,
    ProgrammingLanguage,
    Url,
    WebFramework,
    parse_version,
)

_SOURCE = Url("https://github.com/dokku/dokku")
_DOCS = Url("https://dokku.com/docs/")
dokku_core_block = Manifest(
    name="Dokku Core",
    icon="🚀",
    classification=Classification.cli,
    tags=["paas", "cli", "core"],
    connections=[
        Manifest(name="SSH Gateway"),
        Manifest(name="Git Server"),
        Manifest(name="Docker Scheduler"),
        Manifest(name="Nginx Proxy"),
    ],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "Central PaaS engine (Go + Shell, v0.37.7). Provides the `dokku` CLI, the plugin trigger dispatcher, app lifecycle management (create / deploy / scale / destroy / run), environment config, and the admin HTTP API used by CI integrations and the Dokku Pro dashboard.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Platform control plane\n"
            "\n"
            "Use this block to explain the handoff from **developer intent** to running processes. The CLI coordinates several plugins; a successful command should be investigated in the context of the build, scheduler, and proxy stages it triggered.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Stage | Example evidence | Proposed owner |\n"
            "| --- | --- | --- |\n"
            "| Configuration | App settings and selected plugins | Platform |\n"
            "| Build | Commit reference and image identity | Application team |\n"
            "| Runtime | Process state and readiness result | Platform |\n"
            "| Routing | Host name and upstream mapping | Platform |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Deployment review exercise\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Choose a disposable app and record its starting state.\n"
            "   - Capture the source revision without copying secrets.\n"
            "   - Identify persistent mounts and external dependencies.\n"
            "2. Follow one deployment through builder, scheduler, and proxy.\n"
            "3. Describe how the previous release could be recovered.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "CLI intent -> plugin triggers -> build -> schedule -> route\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> This checklist illustrates platform review; it does not certify a production deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Assign a rollback owner\n"
            "- [ ] Separate app configuration from release artifacts\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - `chi`\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Go tooling for builds and tests\n"
            "  - gofmt for source formatting\n"
            "  - Delve for local debugging\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("0.37.7"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.go],
        frameworks=[WebFramework.chi],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.bare_metal],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[MetricTool.prometheus, MetricTool.grafana, MetricTool.loki],
        links=[
            Link(site_name="Dokku Docs", http_url=_DOCS),
            Link(site_name="Source", http_url=_SOURCE),
        ],
    ),
)
ssh_gateway_block = Manifest(
    name="SSH Gateway",
    icon="🔑",
    classification=Classification.network_gateway,
    tags=["ssh", "auth", "access-control"],
    connections=[Manifest(name="Git Server")],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "SSH server layer built on `sshcommand`. Authenticates incoming connections using stored public keys (`dokku ssh-keys:add`), then translates the git push command into a dokku deploy trigger — without granting shell access to the server.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Deployment identity boundary\n"
            "\n"
            "The gateway links a **public-key identity** to a deployment request. During a sample investigation, distinguish failed authentication from an accepted connection whose downstream build later failed.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Symptom | Suggested evidence | Next boundary |\n"
            "| --- | --- | --- |\n"
            "| Connection refused | Host reachability and SSH listener | Network / host |\n"
            "| Key rejected | Offered key fingerprint and registered identity | Access management |\n"
            "| Push accepted, deploy fails | App name and deployment log | Git Server / App Builder |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Access-review exercise\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Inventory deploy identities for a disposable app.\n"
            "   - Separate a developer's key from a CI automation key.\n"
            "   - Record an accountable owner and removal condition.\n"
            "2. Exercise key removal using a dedicated test identity.\n"
            "3. Verify that other authorized deployment paths still work.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "public key -> identity check -> restricted command -> deploy handoff\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> Suggested checks only. Do not paste private keys or full credential material into an incident note.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Document key rotation ownership\n"
            "- [ ] Test the denied-access path as well as successful deployment\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - ShellCheck for script analysis\n"
            "  - shfmt for formatting\n"
            "  - Bats for shell regression tests\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("0.37.7"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.bash],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.bare_metal],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[MetricTool.prometheus, MetricTool.grafana, MetricTool.loki],
        links=[
            Link(
                site_name="User Mgmt Docs",
                http_url=Url("https://dokku.com/docs/deployment/user-management/"),
            )
        ],
    ),
)
git_server_block = Manifest(
    name="Git Server",
    icon="📦",
    classification=Classification.internal_api,
    tags=["git", "vcs", "deploy-trigger"],
    connections=[Manifest(name="App Builder")],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "Bare git repository manager (Go plugin). Maintains one bare repo per app under `/var/lib/dokku/`. On `git push`, the post-receive hook fires and passes the source archive to the build pipeline.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Source-to-build handoff\n"
            "\n"
            "This component is the source intake point. For a sample release, keep the **commit identity**, target application, and build result together so an operator can distinguish an uploaded revision from the revision currently serving traffic.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Identity | Why record it? |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Target app | Prevent confusion between preview and production destinations |\n"
            "| Commit reference | Connect the deployment to reviewed source |\n"
            "| Build result | Distinguish accepted source from a runnable artifact |\n"
            "| Active release | Establish what users actually receive |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Trace a sample push\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Identify the intended application and remote destination.\n"
            "   - Review branch selection.\n"
            "   - Check that ignored local files are not required to build.\n"
            "2. Follow the source handoff to App Builder.\n"
            "3. Compare the resulting release with the active runtime.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "developer commit -> app repository -> source archive -> App Builder\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> A successful source upload is not, by itself, proof that deployment completed.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Capture the revision in release notes\n"
            "- [ ] Practice diagnosing a deliberately failed test build\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Go tooling for builds and tests\n"
            "  - gofmt for source formatting\n"
            "  - Delve for local debugging\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("0.37.7"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.go],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.bare_metal],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[MetricTool.prometheus, MetricTool.grafana, MetricTool.loki],
        links=[
            Link(
                site_name="Git Deploy Docs",
                http_url=Url("https://dokku.com/docs/deployment/methods/git/"),
            )
        ],
    ),
)
app_builder_block = Manifest(
    name="App Builder",
    icon="🔨",
    classification=Classification.job_processor,
    tags=["buildpack", "docker", "image-build"],
    connections=[Manifest(name="Docker Scheduler")],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "Pluggable build subsystem. Default builder is Herokuish — auto-detects language via official Heroku Buildpacks and compiles a Docker image. Alternatives include Dockerfile, Cloud Native Buildpacks (pack), Nixpacks, and Railpack. Outputs a tagged Docker image pushed to the local daemon.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Reproducible artifact exercise\n"
            "\n"
            "The builder converts source into an image. Use this sample to compare **build inputs** with **runtime configuration**: compiler dependencies belong to the former, while environment-specific settings should be reviewed separately.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Input | Suggested review |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Source revision | Is the intended commit being built? |\n"
            "| Builder selection | Is detection deliberate and documented? |\n"
            "| Dependency lockfiles | Can the same dependency graph be reconstructed? |\n"
            "| Build cache | Does a clean build produce the same application behavior? |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Diagnose a build failure\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Locate the earliest failing build step.\n"
            "   - Separate dependency download errors from compiler failures.\n"
            "   - Redact credentials before sharing logs.\n"
            "2. Reproduce with the same source and builder inputs.\n"
            "3. Confirm the image starts before investigating proxy routing.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "source + builder + dependencies -> image -> Docker Scheduler\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> These are proposed troubleshooting steps; no reproducibility guarantee is implied.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Record builder and runtime versions\n"
            "- [ ] Compare cached and clean builds in a test environment\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Go tooling for builds and tests\n"
            "  - gofmt for source formatting\n"
            "  - Delve for local debugging\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("0.37.7"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.go],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.bare_metal],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[MetricTool.prometheus, MetricTool.grafana, MetricTool.loki],
        links=[
            Link(
                site_name="Builders Docs",
                http_url=Url("https://dokku.com/docs/deployment/builders/builder-management/"),
            ),
            Link(site_name="Herokuish", http_url=Url("https://github.com/gliderlabs/herokuish")),
        ],
    ),
)
docker_scheduler_block = Manifest(
    name="Docker Scheduler",
    icon="🐳",
    classification=Classification.scheduler,
    tags=["scheduler", "containers", "runtime"],
    connections=[Manifest(name="Nginx Proxy")],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "Default container scheduler (`scheduler-docker-local`). Runs app processes defined in `Procfile` as Docker containers on the local daemon, enforces resource limits, performs zero-downtime deploy checks, and manages persistent storage mounts.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Runtime lifecycle\n"
            "\n"
            "Once an image exists, the scheduler owns its process lifecycle. In this sample, examine **startup**, **readiness**, and **steady-state operation** as separate stages; a process that exists may still be unable to serve a useful request.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Stage | Suggested observation | Failure example |\n"
            "| --- | --- | --- |\n"
            "| Start | Exit status and startup log | Missing required setting |\n"
            "| Ready | Application readiness result | Dependency unavailable |\n"
            "| Serve | Error rate and resource use | Memory pressure under load |\n"
            "| Replace | Old and new process behavior | Long requests interrupted |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Replacement exercise\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Record process types and required persistent mounts.\n"
            "   - Identify which paths are disposable.\n"
            "   - Check ownership expectations for mounted data.\n"
            "2. Deploy a test image with a deliberately slow startup.\n"
            "3. Observe when routing changes and what happens to in-flight work.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "image -> start process -> readiness decision -> proxy upstream\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> Exercise guidance only; continuity depends on app behavior and deployment configuration.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Test graceful termination\n"
            "- [ ] Set and review resource budgets\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Go tooling for builds and tests\n"
            "  - gofmt for source formatting\n"
            "  - Delve for local debugging\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("0.37.7"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.go],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.bare_metal],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[MetricTool.prometheus, MetricTool.grafana, MetricTool.loki],
        links=[
            Link(
                site_name="Scheduler Docs",
                http_url=Url("https://dokku.com/docs/deployment/schedulers/docker-local/"),
            )
        ],
    ),
)
cron_scheduler_block = Manifest(
    name="Cron Scheduler",
    icon="⏰",
    classification=Classification.scheduler,
    tags=["cron", "tasks", "scheduler"],
    connections=[Manifest(name="Docker Scheduler")],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "Manages scheduled one-off tasks declared in `app.json` (cron section). Writes systemd crontab entries per app and fires `dokku run` containers on schedule, with full log capture.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Scheduled work and repeatability\n"
            "\n"
            "Scheduled jobs need an outcome that can be inspected after the process exits. For this sample, document **when a job should run**, what it changes, and what a safe retry means.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Concern | Proposed question |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Schedule | Which timezone determines the intended run time? |\n"
            "| Overlap | What happens if one run has not finished before the next starts? |\n"
            "| Retry | Can the same business operation run twice safely? |\n"
            "| Evidence | Where are start time, completion time, and exit status recorded? |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Job rehearsal\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Choose a harmless job against disposable data.\n"
            "   - Observe one successful run.\n"
            "   - Introduce a controlled dependency failure.\n"
            "2. Compare failure reporting with the success record.\n"
            "3. Document how to resume without duplicating completed work.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "scheduled time -> one-off container -> work -> exit status + log\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> Proposed exercises; the sample does not promise exactly-once execution.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Define a maximum expected runtime\n"
            "- [ ] Assign an owner for missed or failed runs\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Go tooling for builds and tests\n"
            "  - gofmt for source formatting\n"
            "  - Delve for local debugging\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("0.37.7"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.go],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.bare_metal],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[MetricTool.prometheus, MetricTool.grafana, MetricTool.loki],
        links=[
            Link(
                site_name="Cron Docs",
                http_url=Url("https://dokku.com/docs/processes/scheduled-cron-tasks/"),
            )
        ],
    ),
)
nginx_proxy_block = Manifest(
    name="Nginx Proxy",
    icon="⚙️",
    classification=Classification.network_gateway,
    tags=["proxy", "routing", "tls"],
    connections=[],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "Default HTTP/HTTPS reverse proxy (`nginx-vhosts` plugin). Renders per-app nginx vhost configs on every deploy, routes `$APP.domain.tld` to the running container port, upgrades WebSocket connections, and terminates TLS. Caddy, Traefik, HAProxy, and OpenResty are plug-in alternatives.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Public routing boundary\n"
            "\n"
            "The proxy joins a public host name to a running application. In this diagram, inspect **DNS**, **TLS**, and **upstream selection** separately so an unreachable hostname is not confused with an unhealthy container.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Observation | Suggested investigation |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Wrong site appears | Host header and virtual-host selection |\n"
            "| TLS handshake fails | Certificate names, expiry, and served chain |\n"
            "| Gateway error | Upstream address, port, and readiness |\n"
            "| WebSocket disconnect | Upgrade handling and timeout behavior |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Routing walkthrough\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Pick a disposable app hostname.\n"
            "   - Follow it from public request to proxy configuration.\n"
            "   - Match the upstream to the intended running process.\n"
            "2. Compare ordinary HTTP and long-lived connections.\n"
            "3. Repeat the checks after a test release.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "hostname + path -> virtual host -> upstream port -> application\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> Review prompts only. Routing and timeout policies depend on local configuration.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Check error pages and request-size limits\n"
            "- [ ] Document where access logs are collected\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Container logs for process diagnostics\n"
            "  - Resource metrics for capacity review\n"
            "  - Versioned configuration for repeatable environments\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("1.27.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.c],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.bare_metal],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[MetricTool.prometheus, MetricTool.grafana, MetricTool.loki],
        links=[
            Link(
                site_name="Proxy Docs",
                http_url=Url("https://dokku.com/docs/networking/proxies/nginx/"),
            )
        ],
    ),
)
certs_plugin_block = Manifest(
    name="Certs Plugin",
    icon="🔒",
    classification=Classification.worker,
    tags=["tls", "certs", "security"],
    connections=[Manifest(name="Nginx Proxy")],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "TLS certificate manager. Stores and applies per-app or wildcard certs (`dokku certs:add`). Integrates with the community `dokku-letsencrypt` plugin for automatic ACME certificate issuance and renewal via the Nginx HTTP-01 challenge.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Certificate lifecycle\n"
            "\n"
            "A certificate has a lifecycle beyond initial installation: issuance, distribution, serving, renewal, and retirement. Use the sample to explain how **certificate material** reaches the proxy and how operators would notice a renewal failure.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Check | Proposed evidence |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Identity | Hostnames included in the certificate |\n"
            "| Validity | Expiration date and intended renewal window |\n"
            "| Delivery | Certificate actually served by the public endpoint |\n"
            "| Renewal | Last successful renewal and actionable failure record |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Renewal rehearsal\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Use a test domain and an isolated certificate workflow.\n"
            "   - Check name resolution and challenge routing.\n"
            "   - Identify who can access private key material.\n"
            "2. Simulate a failed validation without affecting a live hostname.\n"
            "3. Confirm that an operator can locate and understand the failure.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "issue / renew -> store certificate -> proxy reload -> served certificate\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> Suggested lifecycle exercise, not a claim that automatic renewal is configured.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Assign an expiry-alert owner\n"
            "- [ ] Verify the served chain after replacement\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Go tooling for builds and tests\n"
            "  - gofmt for source formatting\n"
            "  - Delve for local debugging\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("0.37.7"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.go],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.bare_metal],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[MetricTool.prometheus, MetricTool.grafana, MetricTool.loki],
        links=[
            Link(site_name="SSL Docs", http_url=Url("https://dokku.com/docs/configuration/ssl/"))
        ],
    ),
)
plugin_system_block = Manifest(
    name="Plugin System",
    icon="🧩",
    classification=Classification.sdk,
    tags=["plugins", "extensibility", "hooks"],
    connections=[Manifest(name="Dokku Core")],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "Bash-based plugin trigger and lifecycle system. Installs community plugins from git URLs (`dokku plugin:install`), manages plugin updates, and dispatches named trigger hooks (50+ built-in triggers) to all registered plugins in priority order, enabling the full plugin ecosystem.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Extension and compatibility review\n"
            "\n"
            "Plugins expand the platform's behavior at lifecycle boundaries. For a sample extension, document **which trigger it handles**, which inputs it reads, and whether a failure should stop deployment or merely report a warning.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Review area | Proposed question |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Source | Who maintains the plugin and which revision is installed? |\n"
            "| Ordering | Does its behavior depend on another trigger handler? |\n"
            "| Side effects | Which host files, services, or application settings can change? |\n"
            "| Upgrade | How will compatibility and rollback be tested? |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Extension exercise\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Inspect a plugin in a disposable environment.\n"
            "   - Map its trigger entry points.\n"
            "   - Record expected outputs and failure behavior.\n"
            "2. Run a deployment with the extension enabled.\n"
            "3. Compare behavior after a controlled plugin failure.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "lifecycle event -> ordered handlers -> side effects -> result\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> Treat these as review prompts; installing an extension requires its own operational assessment.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Record the installed revision\n"
            "- [ ] Rehearse removal and recovery before relying on the extension\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - ShellCheck for script analysis\n"
            "  - shfmt for formatting\n"
            "  - Bats for shell regression tests\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
